clean_summary:
Look, I may be biased, but I think you should check out this fantastic article.

@_xjdr ran his whole lab on NCode for six months: about 25 million lines of code, dozens of services, semi-supervised agents. It's open source and allows any model to be pointed at an OpenAI-compatible endpoint.

The key insight is that you can't cleanly split the model from the software driving it. A smaller model with the right tooling can often outperform a larger one running blindly. NCode provides a tuned setup that is readable and modifiable, with every model earning its tier through months of real-world use across live workloads.

